# j_donuts_app — Clean Architecture

Flutter app structured by **Clean Architecture**, feature-first. Dependencies point **inward**: outer layers depend on inner abstractions, never the reverse.

## Tech stack (fixed)

| Area | Choice |
|------|--------|
| State management + DI | **Riverpod** (providers are the composition root; no services created in widgets) |
| Local database | **Drift** (SQLite), versioned migrations, seeded from bundled JSON |
| Session | `flutter_secure_storage` |
| Navigation | `go_router` (auth redirect guard, `/product/:id`) |
| Models | Immutable: `freezed` + `json_serializable` (or Dart 3 sealed classes/records) |
| Errors | Typed failures via a `Result` type; never swallow exceptions |
| Images | `cached_network_image` + bundled seed assets |
| Connectivity | `connectivity_plus` + real reachability check |
| Strings | `gen-l10n` (ARB files in `lib/l10n/`) |
| Network (only if server added) | Dio with timeout, retry, logging interceptors |

## Layer map

| Layer | Folder (per feature) | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------------|----------------|
| **View (presentation)** | `presentation/` | Pages, widgets, Riverpod notifiers orchestrating UI |
| **Domain** | `domain/` | Entities, repository **interfaces**, use cases, pure validators — no Flutter, no HTTP, no DB |
| **Network** | `data/datasources/remote/` | API clients, DTOs, mappers to entities |
| **Persistence** | `data/datasources/local/` | Drift tables/DAOs, secure storage; mappers to entities |
| **Data glue** | `data/repositories/` | Implements domain repositories; local DB is the **single source of truth** |

```
lib/
  core/
    theme/              # design tokens: colors, typography, spacing
    constants/          # app_colors.dart, app_motion.dart (durations/curves), dimens
    errors/             # Failure, Result
    network/
    di/                 # shared providers (db, connectivity, router)
  l10n/                 # app_en.arb, (app_my.arb bonus)
  features/             # auth, home, product, rewards
    <feature>/
      domain/
      data/
      presentation/
        pages/          # thin screens
        widgets/        # small, composable pieces
        providers/      # Riverpod notifiers + immutable state
test/                   # mirrors lib/
```

- Shared UI goes in `core/widgets/` only when used by **2+** features.
- Files ~300 lines max, functions ~20 lines max; named constants, no magic numbers.

## State management (Riverpod)

- Business rules live in **use cases**/domain, not in widgets or notifiers.
- Notifiers (`AsyncNotifier`/`Notifier`) in `presentation/providers/` call use cases through provider-injected interfaces.
- Expose `AsyncValue` or sealed state: loading / data / error / empty must all be handled on every screen and section.
- Domain exposes repository interfaces; `core/di` or feature providers bind implementations. Tests override providers with fakes.
- Drift watch queries → `Stream` → `StreamProvider`/`AsyncNotifier` so UI updates from DB.

## Screens and widgets

- **Pages** are thin (~< 80 lines): layout + wiring only.
- Break screens into **small single-purpose widgets** in `presentation/widgets/`; combine in the page.
- Pass data/callbacks via constructors so widgets mount in isolation.
- Prefer `StatelessWidget`/`ConsumerWidget`; local `StatefulWidget` only for ephemeral UI (animation, focus).
- Respect Reduce Motion (`MediaQuery.disableAnimations`); animation durations/curves come from the motion constants file.

## Testability (required)

- Every use case, validator, repository impl, mapper, and non-trivial widget has a test mirroring `lib/` under `test/`.
- Validators are **pure functions in domain**, one unit test per rule.
- Depend on abstractions (`abstract class XRepository`); inject fakes via provider overrides.
- Drift tests use in-memory databases; widget tests use no live network or disk.
- Test names describe behaviour. Add one integration test: Register → Home → Product detail.

## Strings and colors

- **No hardcoded** user-visible strings or colors in widgets or logic.
- Strings: ARB files via `gen-l10n`; widgets use `context.l10n.<key>` / `AppLocalizations`.
- Colors/type/spacing: theme tokens in `core/theme` and `core/constants/app_colors.dart`; widgets use `Theme`/`AppColors` only.
- Domain/data have no `BuildContext`: they return typed failures/codes; **presentation maps them to localized text**.

## Dependency rules

```dart
// ✅ GOOD — widget reads a provider; provider uses a use case interface
class HomePage extends ConsumerWidget {
  const HomePage({super.key});
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final home = ref.watch(homeProvider);
    return home.when(data: HomeContent.new, loading: HomeSkeleton.new, error: HomeError.new);
  }
}

// ❌ BAD — widget touches API/DB directly or hardcodes copy/colors
Text('Welcome', style: TextStyle(color: Color(0xFFE91E63)));
```

- **Do**: map DTO/DB row → entity in data before domain sees it.
- **Don’t**: import `presentation/` from `domain/` or `data/`; import Flutter in `domain/`.
- **Don’t**: hardcode data in widgets (automatic fail); commit secrets or client design images.

## New feature checklist

1. `domain/`: entities, repository interface, use cases, validators.
2. `data/`: Drift DAO/remote source, mappers, repository impl.
3. Providers for DI wiring.
4. `presentation/`: notifier + state, page, small widgets; strings in ARB, colors from theme.
5. Tests: unit (domain/data) + widget (presentation).
6. `flutter analyze` clean.
